  "cross_tradition_view": "Most of these traditions would likely judge knowingly misreporting how the speaker was damaged as a failure of honesty or good faith, and potentially justice toward the seller. Compassion might temper blame if the customer was confused or acted without malice, but it would not generally make the inaccurate claim itself truthful or fair.",
